==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Mystic Uril''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Esoteric Uril''' when obtained from [[Infernal Tower]] [[Infernal Tower/Floor 50|Floor 50]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Master Uril's main selling point is that he has a high slow uptime, bringing short-ranged Relics like [[Oldhorn]] and [[Sir Rel]] to a crawl, and his low DPS allows him to be stacked, making him even more effective by paralyzing the vast majority of them so your attackers can burst them down.

Since his [[Surge Attack]] is disconnected from his main attack, it is possible to use Master Uril as a sniper. He is, however, not recommended for that due to his low DPS for his cost. This somewhat limits his usage to Relic enemies, but he works against most of them and makes a huge difference, unless he can easily be reached by attacks for any reason, usually involving support from [[:Category:Long Distance Enemies|Long Distance enemies]].

==='''True Form'''===
True Form grants Esoteric Uril a number of buffs that turn him into an incredible unit. For starters, he gains an HP and damage boost, finally giving him the stats needed for general usage. Esoteric Uril has 88K HP and 4.8K DPS at Lv.30—almost matching the general DPS of units such as [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Urs & Minka]], and far exceeding their health. While that may not seem impressive on paper, his Surge Attacks give his damage a lingering effect that persists until his next attack, effectively creating an area of denial for peons such as Sir Rel or [[Sinner Snache]]. This works incredibly well at clearing the way for [[:Category:Single Attack Cats|Single Attack units]], like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]].

[[Strong Against]] increases his stats immensely, reaching 176K HP and 7.2K DPS vs. Relics and Aku at Lv.30 (280K and 11.5K at Lv.50). Given the abundance of Relic/Aku enemies in the late-game, Esoteric Uril dominates in his niche, providing reliable crowd-control while operating as a damage outlet on his own. This role compression is especially powerful given the near-100% uptime on his [[Slow]] ability. The effect also carries over into his Surge Attacks, making it almost impossible for anything without a [[Shield]] to reach him. [[Curse]], while not as powerful, is a welcome bonus that can help in utilizing non-[[:Category:Cats with Curse Immunity|Curse-Immune]] counters against Relics with multiple traits, mixed Relic stages, as well as countering a few Akus with pesky abilities like [[Wicked Face]].

While most Behemoths within and outside of his targets are Immune to Surges, [[Behemoth Slayer]] is another extremely versatile ability that scales his specialist DPS even higher against Behemoths who aren't resistant. He can easily hold his ground against [[Crustaceous Scissorex]] and [[Crocodylidae Kurocroc]] for extended periods of time whilst you work to eliminate them. He acts as a stable source of pierce that continuously juggles [[Lophiiformes Angaburu]] semi-consistently. And he is a necessity in many strategies that aim to burst down [[Xenobeast Bunaglios]]. This isn't even mentioning his performance against targeted Behemoths who aren't Surge Immune, where it is an absolute slaughterhouse in Uril's favor. He completely wipes the floor with [[Vermilingua Rangmaster]]'s HP using his 28.7K effective DPS at Lv.50, and tanks [[THE FOLIVOREAN]] well enough to chunk him while disabling his Freeze. The Relic side of things isn't as favorable, since [[Ancient Magamojoe]] is immune, and [[Iguanidae Ibilujon]] has Counter-Surge to combat him, necessitating a strategy built around units who aren't affected. But he is still vital in the fight against [[Great Ape Luza]], being the single-best counter to his stages.

These buffs to his survivability and damage make him one of the most important units to unlock in the entire game. His short cooldown means you can even stack multiple of them at any given time too. At that point, Relic and Aku enemies be damned. Overall, Uril's True Form is certainly worth the challenge to conquer the [[Infernal Tower]].

