==Trivia==
*The name Uril may be derived from [[wikipedia:Uriel|Uriel]], a figure in Jewish and Christian religions who is considered a master of knowledge and wisdom. Uriel is an archangel, which may relate to how Mystic Uril is said to have sealed away the demon king.
*He is a reference to [[wikia:dragonball:Dende|Dende]], a character from ''[[wikia:dragonball:Main Page|Dragon Ball]]''. In addition to Uril and Dende having similar designs, [[Heavenly Tower]] [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 50|Floor 50]] resembles [[wikia:dragonball:The Lookout|Kami's Lookout]], which is overtaken by Dende.
**Master Uril's attack animation is also similar to the [[wikia:dragonball:Evil Containment Wave|Evil Containment Wave]], which was used against [[wikia:dragonball:King Piccolo|Great Demon King Piccolo]] like how Mystic Uril is said to have sealed away the demon king.
*Master Uril is implied to be related to [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]] and [[Masked Yulala (Special Cat)|Masked Yulala]]; all three have white and spiky hair, wear tribal masks and joined the Cat Army on their own volition, and both Uril and Yulala reside in the Heavenly Tower.
**Mystic Uril's description indicates that his grandchild gave him his mask. Since Ururun Wolf wears a similar-looking mask, Ururun is most likely Uril's granddaughter, and since Ururun is implied to be Yulala's daughter, Uril is most likely Yulala's father. Furthermore, [[Mystic Mask Yulala]]'s Japanese description calls him the head of his clan, and [[Master Uril (Enemy)|enemy Master Uril]]'s Japanese description says he passed down that same title to his son when he retired.
*Mystic Uril's description makes the first reference to a "demon king" in [[The Battle Cats]], with the second being [[Possessed by Evil (Merciless)|Possessed by Evil]]'s Japanese name (Possessed by the Demon King) and the third being [[Sathankhamun VIII]]'s Japanese description ("A [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Devil]] created during the plan for the second coming of the great demon king via a mask that sealed magical power.").
**This could potentially refer to [[Lord of Ruin Jagando]], who was "once sealed away by great heroes", or [[Infernal Tyrant Nyandam]], who is known as the "Great Demon King" in [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]].
*Ururun Wolf's, Masked Yulala's, Master Uril's and [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Urs & Fenrir]]'s Japanese descriptions all start with a quote followed by how they joined the Cat Army, which always includes the word 勝手 (''katte'', meaning "selfish", "self-serving" or "acting on one's own without asking").

